<title>ARGENTINA: YPF's unit Maxus to name Rosso as CEO.</title>
<headline>YPF's unit Maxus to name Rosso as CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine oil company YPF SA's wholly owned subsidiary Maxus Energy Corp will name current general manager of Maxus Indonesia Mario Rosso as chief executive officer, a YPF spokesman said Thursday.</p>
<p>Rosso, 55, born in Italy, will succeed Roberto Monti, who will be named YPF's CEO and executive vice president soon after a YPF's shareholders meeting called for April 30 names a new board.</p>
<p>((-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
